WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.730
- [Narrator] These two
brilliantly colored monkeys

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.810
are the pride of their
native country, Brazil.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.022
This is the Golden Lion Tamarin.

00:00:08.022 --> 00:00:10.439
(soft music)

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.360
The Golden Lion Tamarin's
signature feature

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.810
is its silky reddish gold coat.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.330
Its long mane frames its bare face,

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.830
thus the feline namesake.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.580
These little guys love
to eat fruits, insects

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.110
and small invertebrates.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.849
And they'll use their long thin fingers

00:00:28.849 --> 00:00:32.300
to hunt for their prey in narrow spaces.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.340
They spend their lives
swinging in the trees

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.460
of Brazil's southeastern coastal forests.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.940
In the 1970s, only a couple
hundred were left in the wild

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.520
due to collection for the
pet trade and habitat loss.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.090
While still endangered today,

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.980
conservation efforts around the world

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.080
have boosted their population.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.990
The Golden Lion Tamarin has
become a national symbol

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:56.660
in Brazil, even appearing
on the country's money.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.063
This is the Golden Lion Tamarin.

